text Classes have ended. There is only homeroom to go before school's out...
text I have already left the classroom.
text I feel that if we end up going home at the same time, then I would be obligated to talk to her...
text I was also terrified of the thought that she might perhaps come up to me herself.
text And so I ditched homeroom, and left the classroom first.
text I am such a coward that I even believe...
text ...perhaps if I just keep running away, it'll all naturally come to an end...
text I sigh at myself for thinking that way, and take a sip of bitter coffee.
text Not being accustomed to the taste, I shudder.
