text Gradually, the sun hangs lower and lower, stretching out the shadows on the ground.
text The linoleum flooring of the hallway is also dyed crimson by the sunset.
text I wonder why red, a color that's supposed to be lively and intense, becomes so melancholic on occasions like this...?
text I rub my knees, which are trembling from exhaustion, while I lean against the wall.
text I still... haven't found her...
text Is she really still here in school...?
text I let out a sigh...
text It's a big, deep sigh... a sigh reflecting my exhaustion.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text @[Tomoya]
text ...!!?
music ~
text The moment I look outside the window, it feels as if my blood has frozen.
text In the crimson-tinted courtyard, there stands somebody.
text Her hair flutters among the wind... I recognize that!
text @[Tomoya]
text (─Ryou!)
